{"abstract":[{"text":"How one helper source tree becomes two binaries, and how each feature finds out whether it can run.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"HeadwireMacKit"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"The App Store and Direct builds"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/headwiremackit\/helperbuilds"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuilds","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Headwire Helper ships in two builds from the same code:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"The App Store build","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is sandboxed and has everything that needs no private API, input included. It is the default: a plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift build"},{"type":"text","text":" makes it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Direct build","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is signed with Developer ID, notarized and unsandboxed. It adds only the code compiled under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HEADWIRE_PRIVATE_API"},{"type":"text","text":": the virtual display that extends the Mac onto the device or gives a Mac with no display one, Apple’s Sidecar started from the menu, and answering the Mac’s side of Bluetooth pairing without a system dialog. Each of these is checked at run time and turns off rather than crashes when macOS has changed it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Helper input is compiled under a second switch, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HEADWIRE_HELPER_INPUT"},{"type":"text","text":", which is on by default in both builds and is turned off only should App Review refuse event posting. A build without it keeps streaming and shows input as unavailable."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This documentation is generated from the App Store build, so the Direct build’s private-API types do not appear in it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Which build is running","anchor":"Which-build-is-running"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuild\/current"},{"type":"text","text":" reads the two compile-time switches and reports the build’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuild\/Distribution-swift.enum"},{"type":"text","text":" and whether helper input is compiled in. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuild\/launchLine(version:dryRun:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the first line the helper logs at launch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Whether a feature runs","anchor":"Whether-a-feature-runs"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperFeatures\/resolve(_:grants:build:macOSHasVirtualDisplay:)"},{"type":"text","text":" combines three inputs into one "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState"},{"type":"text","text":" for each feature:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The menu’s switch for it, in "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperToggles"},{"type":"text","text":". Every switch starts off: the helper is optional, and streaming, input and extending the Mac begin only when the person turns them on."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What macOS has granted, in "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/PermissionGrants"},{"type":"text","text":". A switch that is on without its permission is "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState\/needs(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Onboarding"},{"type":"text","text":" walks the person through that one permission."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What the build contains, and what this macOS still has of it. A feature the build lacks is "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState\/unavailable(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" with an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Unavailability"},{"type":"text","text":" whose "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Unavailability\/menuText"},{"type":"text","text":" is shown on the greyed-out control. The extended display calls a private macOS interface, which the helper checks once a launch; a macOS that renamed or retyped any of it makes the feature "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Unavailability\/notOnThisMacOS"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The extended display also needs streaming, so with its switch on and streaming not running it is "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState\/needsStreaming"},{"type":"text","text":". The features go to the device as the helper’s capabilities, so the device greys out the same controls with the same reasons."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit"]]},"references":{"doc://HeadwireMacKit/documentation/HeadwireMacKit/Unavailability":{"role":"symbol","title":"Unavailability","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Unavailability","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwiremackit\/unavailability","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why this build cannot do a feature."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Unavailability","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Unavailability","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://HeadwireMacKit/documentation/HeadwireMacKit/Onboarding":{"role":"symbol","title":"Onboarding","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Onboarding","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwiremackit\/onboarding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The permission steps the helper’s menu walks a person through."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Onboarding","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Onboarding","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://HeadwireMacKit/documentation/HeadwireMacKit/HelperToggles":{"role":"symbol","title":"HelperToggles","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HelperToggles","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/headwiremackit\/helpertoggles","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The helper’s menu switches. All start off: the helper is optional, and streaming, input and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"letting devices extend this Mac begin only when the person turns them on. Asking before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"t